>> servings: 4
>> source: https://www.nemlig.com/opskrifter/gnocchi-brunet-smoersauce-salvie-sproed-prosciutto-98004202

Heat a large #frying pan{} over medium heat and fry the @prosciutto{140%g} for ~crisp{3%minutes} on each side until crisp.

Transfer the prosciutto to a piece of kitchen paper while you prepare the rest of the dish.

Melt the @butter{100%g} slowly in the same pan until it foams.

Rinse the @sage{20%g}, pick the leaves from the stems, finely chop the stems and roughly tear the leaves.

Peel and finely chop the @garlic{2%cloves}.

Add the garlic, sage stems and sage leaves to the foaming butter and let them brown for ~brown{3%minutes} until the butter is golden and smells aromatic.

Grind over the @black pepper{1%pinch} and grate the zest of the @lemon{1} directly into the butter sauce.

Cook the @gnocchi{900%g} for ~boil{3%minutes}, or according to the package instructions. They should still have a bite, as they finish cooking in the sauce.

Lift the gnocchi out of the water with a sieve or slotted spoon and turn them straight into the pan. Scoop up a little of the pasta water with a cup and swirl it into the pan with the gnocchi.

Finely grate the @parmesan{50%g} and fold it into the dish.

Season to taste with juice from the lemon, @salt{1%pinch} and pepper.

Serve the gnocchi in browned butter with the crispy prosciutto on top.
